==English==
===Etymology===
From {{term|read the Riot Act|lang=en||give a formal warning to a riotous assembly by reading a prescribed portion of the {{w|Riot Act}}, UK, 1715-1967}}

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb|head=[[read]] [[(]][[someone]][[)]] [[the]] [[riot]] [[act]]}}

# {{context|idiomatic|lang=en}} To [[scold]] or [[berate]] somebody; to [[reprimand]].
#: ''She really '''read him the riot act''' about his smoking habit.''

